Preamble
This software, documentation, and associated materials (collectively “Materials”) are published publicly by the Owner (travisrvigue-design) to advance reproducible research, auditing, and legitimate scientific collaboration. Distribution is permitted under the terms below, which are expressly protective of public safety, privacy, and lawful use.

Definitions
- “Owner”: travisrvigue-design and their assigns.
- “Recipient”: any individual or entity receiving the Materials under this License.
- “Authorized Use”: use in accordance with Section 1 (Grant of Rights) and all other Sections below.
- “Prohibited Use”: any use described in Section 2 (Restrictions).

1. Grant of Rights
Subject to the terms and conditions of this License, Owner grants Recipient a worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:
  a) Reproduce, study, and run the Materials for non-commercial research, education, or evaluation purposes;
  b) Create and publicly disclose modifications or derivative works for research/education, provided that such modifications:
     i. include a clear banner that the work is derivative and cite the Owner;
     ii. include provenance information (manifest, SHA-256 digests, buildinfo, and signature verification metadata) and preserve original manifest entries.

2. Restrictions (Prohibited Uses)
Recipient MUST NOT use, deploy, distribute, transfer, or otherwise operationalize the Materials for:
  a) any purpose reasonably expected to cause biological harm, facilitate biological weaponization, enable the design, growth, propagation, genetic modification, or dissemination of biological agents, or otherwise enable activities contrary to biosecurity norms;
  b) surveillance, profiling, targeted population control, or law-enforcement activities without documentary prior written authorization from the Owner and documented institutional review and legal approvals;
  c) commercial exploitation, resale, or embedding in closed-source proprietary systems without a separate commercial license from the Owner;
  d) export, re-export, or transfer in violation of applicable export-control, sanctions, or other regulatory regimes.

3. Human-In-The-Loop & Governance Requirements
Any deployment of Materials that produces clinical, public-health, surveillance, or safety-relevant inferences MUST:
  a) implement a verifiable Human-in-the-Loop gating mechanism equivalent to SOP-001 (human approval, logged and cryptographically signed);
  b) preserve and publish audit manifests and signatures for the run(s) used to produce results, subject to privacy and legal constraints;
  c) ensure that appropriate institutional, ethical, and regulatory approvals are obtained prior to operational deployment.

4. Attribution, Notice, and Provenance
Recipient shall:
  a) retain this License and any Owner notices in all copies and substantial portions of the Materials;
  b) include in any public release of derived results a citation to Owner and a link to this repository (or an unambiguous Owner reference if the repo is taken down), and publish manifest.json and signature verification metadata used to produce the presented results, unless prevented by law or privacy obligations.

5. Contribution and Contributor Obligations
Contributors must sign an Author Contribution Agreement or sign-off via a Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO) confirming they have the right to contribute and agree to license their contributions under this License. Owner may require additional Contributor License Agreements (CLAs) for some uses.

6. Termination
This License and rights granted hereunder will terminate immediately upon Recipient’s breach of any material term (including the Restrictions in Section 2) and may be terminated by Owner for any reason with written notice. Upon termination, Recipient must cease use and distribution of the Materials and, where practicable, remove public copies or otherwise make them inaccessible.

